---
import GrooveLayout from '../../../layouts/GrooveLayout.astro';
import Section from '../../../components/Section.astro';
import Cite from '../../../components/groove/Cite.astro';
import { PROJECT_META } from '../../../config';
import { LINKS, ASSETS, PUBLICATION, gasset } from '../../../lib/groove';

const meta = PROJECT_META.groove;

// Citations and BibTeX are verbatim.
const thesisBib = `@mastersthesis{eriksen2025probing,
  title   = {Probing the World for Groove: A Comparative Study of
             Transfer Learning for Drum Audio Style Classification},
  author  = {Eriksen, Trent},
  school  = {Leiden University},
  type    = {{MSc} thesis, Media Technology},
  address = {Leiden, The Netherlands},
  year    = {2025},
  month   = jun
}`;

const lbdBib = `@inproceedings{eriksen2025comparative,
  title     = {A Comparative Study of Transfer Learning for
               Drum Audio Style Classification},
  author    = {Eriksen, Trent and van der Heide, Edwin and Saunders, Robert},
  booktitle = {Extended Abstracts for the Late-Breaking/Demo Session of the
               26th Int. Society for Music Information Retrieval Conf. (ISMIR)},
  address   = {Daejeon, South Korea},
  year      = {2025}
}`;

let n = 0;
const idx = () => String(++n).padStart(2, '0');
---

<GrooveLayout
  current="/publication"
  title="ISMIR 2025"
  description="The ISMIR 2025 Late-Breaking Demo: abstract, paper, poster, video, citation, and acknowledgements."
  label="ISMIR 2025 · Late-Breaking Demo"
  heading="From MSc thesis to ISMIR publication"
  lede="The thesis was condensed into a Late-Breaking Demo presented at the 26th ISMIR conference in Daejeon, South Korea."
>
  <Section
    index={idx()}
    label="Daejeon, South Korea · September 2025"
    title="Presented at the 26th ISMIR"
  >
    <div class="conf">
      <img
        class="conf-photo"
        src={gasset('/figures/ismir-2025-author.webp')}
        width="825"
        height="1100"
        alt="Trent Eriksen holding his ISMIR 2025 author badge in the conference hall, with the 26th ISMIR title screen behind him."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <div>
        <p class="g-lead">
          The Late-Breaking Demo was presented at the 26th International Society for Music
          Information Retrieval Conference. The trip was supported by an ISMIR First-time Authors
          Grant and research grants from Leiden University.
        </p>
        <div class="g-actions">
          <a class="btn" href={LINKS.ismir} rel="noopener">Official ISMIR 2025 page</a>
          <a class="btn" href={LINKS.scholar} rel="noopener">Author on Google Scholar</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section index={idx()} label="Two distinct works">
    <div class="g-grid2 works">
      <article class="work">
        <p class="work-kind">MSc Thesis</p>
        <h2 class="work-title">{PUBLICATION.thesisTitle}</h2>
        <dl class="meta">
          <div><dt>Author</dt><dd>Trent Eriksen</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Degree</dt><dd>{PUBLICATION.degree}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Supervisors</dt><dd>{PUBLICATION.supervisors.join(', ')}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Completed</dt><dd>{PUBLICATION.thesisDate}</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="work-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={ASSETS.thesisPdf}>Read the thesis (PDF)</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="work">
        <p class="work-kind">ISMIR 2025 Late-Breaking Demo</p>
        <h2 class="work-title">{PUBLICATION.lbdTitle}</h2>
        <dl class="meta">
          <div><dt>Authors</dt><dd>Trent Eriksen, Edwin van der Heide, Robert Saunders</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Affiliation</dt><dd>Leiden University Media Technology</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Venue</dt><dd>{PUBLICATION.venue}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Location</dt><dd>{PUBLICATION.venueLocation}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>License</dt><dd>{PUBLICATION.license}</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="work-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={ASSETS.lbdPdf}>LBD paper (PDF)</a>
          <a class="btn" href={LINKS.ismir} rel="noopener">Official ISMIR page</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="g-small g-gap">
      These are separate citations. The Late-Breaking Demo is a short extended abstract derived
      from, but not identical to, the full thesis.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section index={idx()} label="Official abstract · ISMIR 2025 LBD">
    {/* The official abstract, verbatim. */}
    <p class="abstract">
      Research in drum classification often trends in two key directions: (1) audio-based
      single-instrument classification, or (2) automatic drum transcription, which makes exploration
      of drum-audio <em>style</em> compelling, especially in comparison to a CNN trained on the GMD (Groove
      MIDI Dataset) with a pretrained transformer-based model, PaSST (Patchout Audio Spectrogram Transformer),
      with frozen general-audio embeddings from AudioSet. This comparison reveals the ways in which general
      audio knowledge can affect drum-audio style classification. Experiments with model depth, augmentation,
      and padding show that PaSST with these frozen embeddings reduces performance in terms of accuracy
      but reveals a robust feature representation distinct from the CNN.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section index={idx()} label="Presentation" title="Watch the demo">
    <div class="g-video">
      <iframe
        src={`https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/${meta.demoVideoId}?rel=0`}
        title={meta.demoVideoTitle}
        loading="lazy"
        allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
        referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
        allowfullscreen></iframe>
    </div>
    <p class="g-small">
      Hosted on YouTube · also linked from the <a href={LINKS.ismir} rel="noopener"
        >official ISMIR 2025 program page</a
      >.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section index={idx()} label="Cite this work" title="Citation and BibTeX">
    <div class="cites">
      <Cite
        label="Thesis"
        citation="Eriksen, T. (2025). Probing the World for Groove: A Comparative Study of Transfer Learning for Drum Audio Style Classification. MSc thesis, Media Technology, Leiden University."
        bibtex={thesisBib}
      />
      <Cite
        label="ISMIR 2025 LBD"
        citation="Eriksen, T., van der Heide, E., & Saunders, R. (2025). A Comparative Study of Transfer Learning for Drum Audio Style Classification. Extended Abstracts for the Late-Breaking/Demo Session of the 26th ISMIR Conference, Daejeon, South Korea."
        bibtex={lbdBib}
      />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section index={idx()} label="Acknowledgements and support" title="Grants">
    <ul class="g-list">
      <li><strong>ISMIR First-time Authors Grant</strong>, August 2025</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Creative Intelligence and Technology Grant</strong>, Leiden University, September
        2025
      </li>
      <li><strong>Leiden University Fund Research Grant</strong>, October 2025</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="g-small g-gap">
      With thanks to supervisors Edwin van der Heide and Robert Saunders, and to Leiden University
      Media Technology.
    </p>
  </Section>
</GrooveLayout>

<style>
  .conf {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--sp-6);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .conf-photo {
    display: block;
    width: auto;
    max-height: 360px;
    border: var(--hair) solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .conf {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--sp-4);
    }
    .conf-photo {
      max-height: 300px;
    }
  }
  .works {
    align-items: stretch;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .work {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: var(--sp-5);
    border: var(--hair) solid var(--hairline);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .work-kind {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  /* Paper titles keep their own casing: set in the display face, not the uppercase h2 set. */
  .work-title {
    margin: var(--sp-2) 0 var(--sp-4);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    text-transform: none;
    font-stretch: 105%;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .meta {
    flex: 1;
    margin: 0 0 var(--sp-5);
  }
  .meta > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--sp-3);
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: var(--hair) solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .meta dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .meta dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .meta > div {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0.1rem;
    }
  }
  .work-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
  }
  .abstract {
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .cites {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--sp-5);
    max-width: 56rem;
  }
</style>
